WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:03.680
If you want to hear the details about Carrie's&nbsp;
life that weren't included in the movies,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:03.680 --> 00:00:07.680
then stick around to the end of this&nbsp;
video. This video is sponsored by Audible.

00:00:12.480 --> 00:00:16.400
I've covered a lot characters in Stephen&nbsp;
King's universe of stories here on this show,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:16.400 --> 00:00:19.840
so in this week's episode I'm taking&nbsp;
it back to the one that started it all.

00:00:19.840 --> 00:00:23.040
Welcome to Horror History, my name&nbsp;
is Professor CZsWorld and in today's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:23.040 --> 00:00:27.600
lesson I'm joined by my TA, The Amagi, as&nbsp;
we cover the entire life of Carrie White.

00:00:27.600 --> 00:00:32.000
Carrie was created by the then rookie author&nbsp;
as a sort of combination of two girls from his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:35.840
childhood. The first was in grade school with&nbsp;
King, and she was made fun of by some of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:35.840 --> 00:00:39.280
other classmates for wearing the same clothes&nbsp;
to school every day. The other lived in his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:39.280 --> 00:00:42.720
neighborhood with her mother, and one time&nbsp;
the mother hired him to move some furniture,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:42.720 --> 00:00:46.720
and when he went inside her realized they&nbsp;
were crazy religious. Neither one of them&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:46.720 --> 00:00:51.834
would live to read Carrie though, one was personally responsible while the other had problems with seizures.

00:00:51.834 --> 00:00:55.120
Their fates may tie in to what ends&nbsp;
up happening to Carrie, but before we&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:55.120 --> 00:00:59.120
can get there, I'm gonna take it alllll the&nbsp;
way back to the conception of Carrie White.

00:01:04.320 --> 00:01:09.600
Margaret Brigham and Ralph White were married on&nbsp;
March 23rd, 1962 and that same year they first&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:09.600 --> 00:01:13.840
engaged in what Margaret would refer to as 'a&nbsp;
sinful act', so she made she made her husband&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:13.840 --> 00:01:17.440
promise never to do it again. She fell down&nbsp;
one day and lost the baby. And&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:17.440 --> 00:01:21.840
she assumed that this was their punishment for their&nbsp;
sins, that God did not want her to have the baby.

00:01:21.840 --> 00:01:26.080
One night Ralph started giving her that look&nbsp;
again. I’m not gonna do it right here on camera,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:26.080 --> 00:01:28.720
cause I don’t want to be a&nbsp;
father, but she sent him away,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:28.720 --> 00:01:32.480
and when he came back she smelled the&nbsp;
scent of roadhouse whiskey on his breath.

00:01:32.480 --> 00:01:38.146
Nine months later, on September 21st 1963 she gave&nbsp;
birth to Carrietta N White, 

00:01:38.240 --> 00:01:40.640
Margaret’s mental state&nbsp;
deteriorated throughout the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:40.640 --> 00:01:43.760
pregnancy, and she planned&nbsp;
to kill Carrie with a knife upon birth,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:43.760 --> 00:01:47.360
because she believed her daughter would be a&nbsp;
carrier of the devil, but when it came time,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:47.360 --> 00:01:51.200
she could not bring herself to do it, instead&nbsp;
using the knife to cut the umbilical cord.

00:01:51.200 --> 00:01:56.640
She would try again three years later in 1966.&nbsp;
Here’s what went down. Mrs. White had long feuded&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:56.640 --> 00:02:00.960
with her neighbors, the Horan family because their&nbsp;
daughter, Estelle would sometimes sunbathe in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:00.960 --> 00:02:05.840
the backyard, which was within Margaret’s line of&nbsp;
sight. Mrs. Horan found this complaint ridiculous,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:05.840 --> 00:02:09.840
and in retaliation bought Estelle a new&nbsp;
bikini and encouraged her to use it whenever&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:09.840 --> 00:02:14.560
she liked. So 3-year-old Carrie wandered over to a&nbsp;
sunbathing Estelle one day and posed the question.

00:02:14.560 --> 00:02:17.751
“What are thoooooose?!”

00:02:17.751 --> 00:02:20.880
I'm sorry, that was too easy not to&nbsp;
do. When Estelle explained the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:20.880 --> 00:02:24.160
concept of breasts to her, Carrie&nbsp;
wished that she could get them too,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:24.160 --> 00:02:27.440
because her mother had taught her that good&nbsp;
girls don’t get them as part of her wacko&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:27.440 --> 00:02:32.000
religious beliefs. Estelle tried to explain the&nbsp;
truth to Carrie, but not before Margaret came out&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:32.000 --> 00:02:35.600
and started screaming at her, to the point that&nbsp;
Estelle started to get into it with Margaret.

00:02:35.600 --> 00:02:40.160
Mrs. White was clawing at herself, grinning and&nbsp;
drooling in what she saw as punishing herself&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:40.160 --> 00:02:44.160
to make up for what Carrie had seen. This kind&nbsp;
of self destructive behaviour warped Carrie’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:44.160 --> 00:02:47.440
mind from a very young age and caused&nbsp;
her to have an imbalance in her brain&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:47.440 --> 00:02:48.320
as she grew older.

00:02:48.320 --> 00:02:51.920
She drags Carrie into the house and forces&nbsp;
her daughter to go into the closet to pray,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:51.920 --> 00:02:56.000
which Carrie strongly disliked because the&nbsp;
religious imagery scared her. So she did what any&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:56.000 --> 00:03:01.040
kid would do and threw a fit. However Carrie White&nbsp;
was not like any other kid. She was born with a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:01.040 --> 00:03:06.960
special gene that researchers would later refer to&nbsp;
as the TK gene. TK was an acronym for telekinesis,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:06.960 --> 00:03:11.760
the ability to move objects at a distance via the&nbsp;
use of mental power. Both of Carrie’s parents had&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:11.760 --> 00:03:15.200
this gene, but it was recessive in her&nbsp;
mother, so it only showed up in Carrie.

00:03:15.200 --> 00:03:17.760
Carrie’s grandmother was also&nbsp;
supposedly a firestarter,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:17.760 --> 00:03:20.480
an ability that would later be&nbsp;
explored more in another Stephen King novel,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:20.480 --> 00:03:24.320
but it’s not known if the gene for&nbsp;
this is the same as the gene for TK.

00:03:24.320 --> 00:03:28.228
The neighbor, Estelle, heard Carrie’s&nbsp;
screams emanating from inside the&nbsp;house,

00:03:28.228 --> 00:03:31.680
and this is what set Carrie’s telekinesis&nbsp;
off. It started when a huge chunk&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:31.680 --> 00:03:34.640
of ice was pulled down and thumped&nbsp;
against the White’s roof. Then it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:34.640 --> 00:03:38.400
was several chunks of ice, and keep in mind,&nbsp;
this is happening in the middle of August.

00:03:38.400 --> 00:03:42.400
The ice stopped and Margaret started screaming&nbsp;
again. That’s when the White’s kitchen table went&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:42.400 --> 00:03:46.480
crashing out the window, a small sample of the&nbsp;
magnitude of Carrie’s power. She brought down a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:46.480 --> 00:03:50.720
rain of stones upon the house. Neighbors watched&nbsp;
as they burst through the roof shingles, punching&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:50.720 --> 00:03:55.120
holes through the ceiling. The stones consisted&nbsp;
of chunks of granite which only came down on the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:55.120 --> 00:03:59.120
White’s property. The stones that didn’t hit&nbsp;
the house left small craters in the backyard.

00:03:59.120 --> 00:04:02.080
The event became known by the&nbsp;
neighborhood as The Rain of Stones,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:02.080 --> 00:04:05.280
and I think it’s no mistake that it was&nbsp;
triggered by Carrie finding out about&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:05.280 --> 00:04:09.040
the pubescent development of breasts and her&nbsp;
mother punishing her for it. Carrie’s powers&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:09.040 --> 00:04:12.800
would be fully unleashed when she herself&nbsp;
reaches the age of her budding adulthood,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:12.800 --> 00:04:17.520
so there seems to be a comparison going on between&nbsp;
sexual awakening and telekinetic awakening.

00:04:17.520 --> 00:04:20.640
It wouldn’t be the last time Stephen&nbsp;
King would make a similar comparison,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:20.640 --> 00:04:23.680
as you know if you’ve seen my Horror&nbsp;
History on Beverly Marsh from It.

00:04:23.680 --> 00:04:26.720
It seems that Carrie started going&nbsp;
to public school in first grade,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:26.720 --> 00:04:30.160
this may have coincided with her Mom getting&nbsp;
a job at the Blue-Ribbon Laundry when the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:30.160 --> 00:04:33.760
insurance money from Ralph’s death had run&nbsp;
out. Carrie is described as a chunky girl&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:33.760 --> 00:04:37.520
with pimples. None of the movies hold true&nbsp;
to this description, probably because her&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:37.520 --> 00:04:41.440
beauty is supposed to blossom by the time&nbsp;
of the prom… and you can do that in a book,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:41.440 --> 00:04:45.600
but in a movie your best bet it to just hide&nbsp;
her looks until the prom scene comes around.

00:04:45.600 --> 00:04:47.840
Carrie did not get along well in school though and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:47.840 --> 00:04:51.680
quickly became a social outcast. This&nbsp;
was mostly due to her psycho mother and

00:04:51.680 --> 00:04:55.200
the fact that she was forbidden from taking&nbsp;
part in most social activities. She also&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:55.200 --> 00:04:59.680
had a few particularly nasty classmates,&nbsp;
like Christine Hargensen and Helen Shyres.

00:04:59.680 --> 00:05:03.440
In grade school Carrie went to a Christian Youth&nbsp;
Camp where they would short-sheet her bed,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:03.440 --> 00:05:05.600
hide her underwear, put a snake in her shoe,

00:05:05.600 --> 00:05:07.680
“There’s a snake in my boot.”

00:05:07.680 --> 00:05:11.360
...and pass around a love letter addressed&nbsp;
to Flash Bobby Pickett that they’d found in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:11.360 --> 00:05:14.960
Carrie’s possession. If you’re wondering who&nbsp;
Flash Bobby Pickett is… I don’t know where&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:14.960 --> 00:05:18.480
the name “Flash” comes from, that seems to&nbsp;
be exclusive to Carrie... but Bobby Pickett&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:18.480 --> 00:05:22.800
is the guy who wrote the Monster Mash. If&nbsp;
you’re wondering what the Monster Mash is,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:22.800 --> 00:05:27.360
it was a graveyard smash. And if you’re&nbsp;
wondering how it became a graveyard smash,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:27.360 --> 00:05:31.680
it caught on in a flash. Ohhhh kay&nbsp;
maybe that’s where “Flash” came from.

00:05:31.680 --> 00:05:35.120
Carrie had to be brought home from camp a week&nbsp;
early. On her first day of grammar school,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:35.120 --> 00:05:38.480
she was laughed at for praying at&nbsp;
lunch. As you can probably imagine,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:38.480 --> 00:05:42.560
the torture from the other kids and the abuse&nbsp;
from her devil-paranoid mother would continue,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:42.560 --> 00:05:46.640
as Carrie moved onto the next lair of&nbsp;
hell commonly known as middle school.

00:05:50.560 --> 00:05:53.600
There is a lot you can learn here on Horror&nbsp;
History, but if you really want the full&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:53.600 --> 00:05:57.840
Stephen King experience, you gotta check out the&nbsp;
novel. There are so many characters, interviews&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:57.840 --> 00:06:01.360
and snippets from articles from within the world of&nbsp;
Carrie that you’re missing out on if you don’t.

