00:06:54.720 --> 00:06:58.880
One of the few activities that Carrie White was&nbsp;
allowed to partake in were these biking trips.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:58.880 --> 00:07:00.960
Actually, it doesn’t seem&nbsp;
like she really wanted to go,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:00.960 --> 00:07:03.040
but maybe it was a church activity or something.

00:07:03.040 --> 00:07:06.880
In school, a boy named Billy Preston put&nbsp;
peanut butter in her hair. Now according&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:06.880 --> 00:07:10.720
to Rhett and Link he was actually doing her&nbsp;
a favor, but the deep seeded rage continued&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:10.720 --> 00:07:14.400
to build inside of her. People would pinch&nbsp;
her, stick out legs to trip her in class,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:14.400 --> 00:07:17.520
knock books from her desk and tuck&nbsp;
obscene messages into her bag.

00:07:17.520 --> 00:07:21.520
In high school, Chris Hargensen prank called&nbsp;
her, asking if she knew how to spell “pig poop”,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:21.520 --> 00:07:26.800
and spelling K-A-R-R-I-E, which I have to say&nbsp;
is not even that good of a prank call… but&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:26.800 --> 00:07:30.960
I guess this was before iconic masterpieces&nbsp;
like “Arnold Schwarzenegger prank calls&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:30.960 --> 00:07:33.840
travel agency and keeps asking&nbsp;
about the guy they lobotomized”.

00:07:35.920 --> 00:07:37.840
“May I have your email address please?”

00:07:37.840 --> 00:07:39.120
“Yeah. What do you mean, we?”

00:07:40.720 --> 00:07:44.240
“In order to book this, may I&nbsp;
have your email address please?”

00:07:44.240 --> 00:07:47.360
“What about the guy you&nbsp;
lobotomized. Did he get a refund?”

00:07:47.360 --> 00:07:47.860
“What guy?”

00:07:48.106 --> 00:07:49.486
*laughter* 

00:07:51.044 --> 00:07:52.265
I can't...

00:07:52.265 --> 00:07:56.480
 Carrie would have&nbsp;&nbsp;to endure cruel punishments that she did not&nbsp;
deserve, like being locked in the closet for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:56.480 --> 00:08:00.960
an entire day after stealing a 49 cent plastic&nbsp;
ring, and another time when her Mom found a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:00.960 --> 00:08:05.600
picture of Flash Bobby Picket under her pillow.&nbsp;
Guess she reallyyyy likes the Monster Mash….

00:08:05.600 --> 00:08:08.400
At one point in seventh grade, she&nbsp;
seemed to try to call out for help&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:08.400 --> 00:08:11.520
when she turned the following in as&nbsp;
a poetry assignment in English class:

00:08:11.520 --> 00:08:14.880
“Jesus watches from the wall, But&nbsp;
his face is cold as stone, And if&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:14.880 --> 00:08:18.560
he loves me As she tells me&nbsp;
Why do I feel so all alone?”

00:08:18.560 --> 00:08:22.160
This is a piece about her time being locked&nbsp;
inside the closet by her mother, and while&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:22.160 --> 00:08:26.480
the instructor did find that it seemed to cry out&nbsp;
to him, he did not pursue the topic any further.

00:08:26.480 --> 00:08:27.984
But perhaps the biggest moment,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:27.984 --> 00:08:31.600
came during Carrie’s senior year&nbsp;
of high school. Carrie was the last to shower&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:31.600 --> 00:08:35.920
after gym class in an attempt to avoid the other&nbsp;
girls, when she got her period. Like the Rain of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:35.920 --> 00:08:39.680
Stones when she was three, it was her mother’s&nbsp;
neglect to give her a proper education&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:39.680 --> 00:08:43.760
due to Mrs. White’s unsound levels of&nbsp;
piousness that once again caused the issue.

00:08:43.760 --> 00:08:46.800
Carrie believed that she was bleeding to&nbsp;
death, because she’d never learned what&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:46.800 --> 00:08:50.800
a period is. Her mom didn’t teach her, and&nbsp;
she didn’t have any friends to learn from.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:50.800 --> 00:08:54.000
She staggered to the other girls, who were&nbsp;
finishing up getting changed, and they found&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:54.000 --> 00:08:58.640
it hilarious, they basically saw this as the&nbsp;
equivalent of Arnold calling the travel agency.

00:08:58.640 --> 00:09:02.880
“I just need an email address so I&nbsp;
can email you your confirmation.”

00:09:03.680 --> 00:09:09.280
“OK. 2. 3. 5. 7. 2.,”

00:09:09.280 --> 00:09:11.600
Ok sorry. I’m done. I’m done now. OK?

00:09:11.600 --> 00:09:16.400
So the whole gym class started chanting “period”&nbsp;
and throwing tampons at her, and in her confusion,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:16.400 --> 00:09:20.320
Carrie collapsed in the corner. The gym teacher&nbsp;
Ms. Desjardin came in to see what the problem&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:20.320 --> 00:09:24.160
was and ended up slapping Carrie in the face&nbsp;
to try to bring her to her senses. A lightbulb&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:24.160 --> 00:09:28.560
explodes overhead, and this ties Carrie’s&nbsp;
outburst of anger to her telekinetic power.

00:09:28.560 --> 00:09:32.880
Once Ms. Desjardin realized that Carrie didn’t&nbsp;
know what a period was, she tries to comfort&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:32.880 --> 00:09:37.120
her and get the other girls away. She ended up&nbsp;
having to explain the concept of menstruation,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:37.120 --> 00:09:40.640
before getting Carrie cleaned up and taking&nbsp;
her to the office of the Assistant Principal,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:40.640 --> 00:09:44.800
Mr. Morton, where he files an accident form and&nbsp;
decides to give Carrie the rest of the day off.

00:09:44.800 --> 00:09:49.360
Mr. Morton repeatedly calls her Cassie instead of&nbsp;
Carrie one too many times, and she snaps at him.

00:09:49.360 --> 00:09:53.760
“That's not my name!” she screamed suddenly.&nbsp;
Morton recoiled, and Miss Desjardin jumped&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:53.760 --> 00:09:57.360
as if struck from behind. The heavy&nbsp;
ceramic ashtray on Morton's desk (it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:57.360 --> 00:10:00.960
was Rodin's Thinker with his head turned&nbsp;
into a receptacle for cigarette butts)&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:00.960 --> 00:10:04.320
suddenly toppled to the rug, as if to&nbsp;
take cover from the force of her scream.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:04.320 --> 00:10:08.240
Butts and flakes of Morton's pipe tobacco&nbsp;
scattered on the pale-green nylon rug.”

00:10:08.240 --> 00:10:12.880
Like the lightbulb, this is another example of the&nbsp;
fervor of her telekinesis matching the anger pent&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:12.880 --> 00:10:14.240
up inside of her, and with years and years of&nbsp;
bullying and being laughed at, she had a lot of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:14.240 --> 00:10:18.320
anger on hand to dish out pretty much at will,&nbsp;
which we see shortly after as she walked home.

00:10:18.502 --> 00:10:21.120
 At this point,&nbsp;
Carrie is fed up after having endured 17&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:21.120 --> 00:10:24.960
years of harassment. There’s only so much a&nbsp;
person can take, so it’s understandable that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:24.960 --> 00:10:28.967
her thoughts would turn dark. But what&nbsp;
makes this scary is what happens next.

00:10:28.967 --> 00:10:33.221
A five year&nbsp;old boy riding his bike on the street makes&nbsp;
fun of her and calls her Creepy Carrie,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:33.221 --> 00:10:34.960
"Creepy Carrie, Creepy Carrie!"

00:10:34.960 --> 00:10:38.173
so that little ****er get air&nbsp;
yeeted right off that bike.

00:10:48.880 --> 00:10:51.920
Carrie would also try to use her TK&nbsp;
to break a window on the way home,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:51.920 --> 00:10:56.080
but she’s only able to make it wobble, showing&nbsp;
that she’s yet to fully master the ability. She&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:56.080 --> 00:11:00.000
still has to practice more before being able&nbsp;
to fully channel her rage at will, but later&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:00.000 --> 00:11:04.000
that afternoon she was able to crack her mirror&nbsp;
while self-loathing about her own reflection.

00:11:04.000 --> 00:11:07.920
Her mother came home after getting a call from the&nbsp;
school. Carrie notices the fear in her mother’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:07.920 --> 00:11:12.000
eyes. There are a few examples in the book where&nbsp;
Margaret seems to be able to sense Carrie’s rising&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:12.000 --> 00:11:15.920
power, but it’s likely that she perceived it&nbsp;
as the devil inside of her daughter waking up.

00:11:15.920 --> 00:11:19.520
Mrs. White struck her, and forced her head&nbsp;
into the altar they had in the living room,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:19.520 --> 00:11:23.120
commanding her to pray for her sins, to&nbsp;
which she insisted that she had not sinned.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:23.120 --> 00:11:26.720
This was a turning point for Carrie, because up&nbsp;
until now she had no reason not to believe her&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:26.720 --> 00:11:30.560
mother’s lies. She was also about to graduate&nbsp;
high school and didn’t want to live under the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:30.560 --> 00:11:35.280
harmful hand of her mother forever, and that’s why&nbsp;
I think she chooses this occasion to fight back.

00:11:41.360 --> 00:11:45.360
As Margaret tried to pull her daughter away&nbsp;
into the closet, Carrie refused to go quietly,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:45.360 --> 00:11:48.160
raising her voice and using&nbsp;
profanity against her. Again,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:48.160 --> 00:11:51.920
the fear is evident in Margaret’s eyes. Carrie&nbsp;
threatens to make the stones come again,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:51.920 --> 00:11:54.320
remembering the outburst that&nbsp;
had occured when she was three,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:54.320 --> 00:11:58.400
and her mom calls her the spawn of the devil&nbsp;
before dragging her and locking her in the closet.

00:11:58.400 --> 00:12:00.720
This was probably the most she’d&nbsp;
ever fought back against her Mom,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:00.720 --> 00:12:04.160
but I think that's because of that rising&nbsp;
fear, that the punishment is not as severe&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:04.160 --> 00:12:06.960
as Carrie might have thought. Carrie&nbsp;
even thinks that her Momma may have&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:06.960 --> 00:12:11.280
been afraid she’d blow the closet door right&nbsp;
off its hinges if she was kept in too long.

00:12:11.280 --> 00:12:14.480
Carrie took a little bit of time off of&nbsp;
school, and used it to further hone her&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:14.480 --> 00:12:18.000
telekinetic abilities. She would practice&nbsp;
at home in her room by picking up the foot&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:18.000 --> 00:12:22.240
of her bed and placing it back down. Her heart&nbsp;
pounded with excitement as she did so, and at&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:22.240 --> 00:12:26.160
night she would dream of sending stones after&nbsp;
her Mom and the kids at school.

00:12:26.160 --> 00:12:30.320
When she goes back to school, she keeps to&nbsp;
herself even more than usual, hoping to avoid&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:30.320 --> 00:12:34.560
being the subject of laughter and gossip about&nbsp;
what happened, but that Thursday after her fifth&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:34.560 --> 00:12:39.200
period study hall she received a surprise visit&nbsp;
from a boy she was attracted to, Tommy Ross.

00:12:39.200 --> 00:12:41.760
Tommy was the boyfriend of Susan&nbsp;
Snell, one of the girls who had&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:41.760 --> 00:12:44.800
made fun of her in the locker room,&nbsp;
but who was otherwise not normally&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:44.800 --> 00:12:48.560
a bad person. Tommy ended up inviting&nbsp;
her to be his date to the Spring Ball.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:48.560 --> 00:12:52.960
This is the moment I’ve been hyping up in every&nbsp;
Horror History episode to date, so pay attention!

00:12:52.960 --> 00:12:56.720
What happens next is kind of interesting.&nbsp;
It’s not entirely clear if Carrie is able&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:56.720 --> 00:13:00.240
to shine yet. Shining is an ability in&nbsp;
Stephen King’s writing allowing people,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:00.240 --> 00:13:03.920
most often kids, to read minds. She’s able&nbsp;
to do it by the end of the story though.

00:13:03.920 --> 00:13:07.920
Her first instinct is that Tommy is tricking&nbsp;
her, that he’s only inviting her to humiliate&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:07.920 --> 00:13:11.600
her somehow. If she’d been able to shine,&nbsp;
she’d know that his invitation was genuine.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:11.600 --> 00:13:15.840
But perhaps she did shine, and saw that Tommy&nbsp;
didn’t want to ask Carrie to prom, which is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:15.840 --> 00:13:20.320
also true because he was only doing it to please&nbsp;
Sue, who felt bad about the locker room incident.

00:13:20.320 --> 00:13:23.840
For these reasons, Carrie rejects him&nbsp;
at first, but he is persistent about it,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:23.840 --> 00:13:27.600
and she worries she’s going to make him&nbsp;
late for his next class and she accepts.

00:13:27.600 --> 00:13:31.040
That week she goes into town and buys&nbsp;
some fabric to make herself a dress.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:31.040 --> 00:13:33.600
Sewing was one of the few hobbies&nbsp;
her Mom allowed her to have,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:33.600 --> 00:13:37.440
so she was quite familiar with the Chamberlain&nbsp;
Woolworth’s where she bought her material.

00:13:37.440 --> 00:13:39.200
She had not yet broken the news to her mother,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:39.200 --> 00:13:42.800
which caused her a great deal of anxiety&nbsp;
and stress, which of course translated to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:42.800 --> 00:13:43.904
telekinetic energy. 

00:13:44.000 --> 00:13:47.440
On Saturday night, Carrie prepares herself&nbsp;
to tell her mother of the prom invite,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:47.440 --> 00:13:50.320
knowing that she is unlikely&nbsp;
to approve. And she doesn’t.

00:13:54.400 --> 00:13:59.120
Ok, the tea was only lukewarm, but you get the&nbsp;
idea. As expected, Margaret orders her to go to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:59.120 --> 00:14:03.520
the closet, but Carrie refuses, looking to make a&nbsp;
statement. They get into a huge argument, because&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:03.520 --> 00:14:07.405
Margaret sees this as the next step towards a&nbsp;
path to the devil:

00:14:08.726 --> 00:14:16.634
MARGARET: "After the blood come the boys, like sniffing dogs. Grinning and slobbering and trying to find out where that smell comes from.

00:14:16.634 --> 00:14:18.449
Where the smell is. That smell.

00:14:19.624 --> 00:14:24.000
Listen, I know where they take you in their cars, I see it alright. Well you're not going."

00:14:24.000 --> 00:14:27.520
Carrie tells her that she’s tired of being&nbsp;
made fun of and wants to start fitting in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:27.520 --> 00:14:31.280
with her classmates. She wants to live her&nbsp;
own life, not be stuck living her mother's.

00:14:31.280 --> 00:14:34.480
Her Mom calls her a witch, and I&nbsp;
see that as another important step&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:34.480 --> 00:14:38.000
towards Carrie’s breakdown. Even though&nbsp;
her mother did not treat her properly,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:38.000 --> 00:14:41.920
she was still her mother and Carrie knew no&nbsp;
better than to look to and love her -- not&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:41.920 --> 00:14:45.520
to mention that she was one of the only&nbsp;
people Carrie could actually talk to.

00:14:45.520 --> 00:14:48.960
If her mother started to oppose her, she&nbsp;
would have nobody to go to the next time&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:48.960 --> 00:14:53.280
she is humiliated, and be forced to turn down&nbsp;
a darker path… and that day would soon come.

00:14:53.280 --> 00:14:56.880
Margaret retreated upstairs and&nbsp;
began whispering exorcism prayers.

00:14:56.880 --> 00:15:00.960
On May 26th, the day before the prom, Carrie&nbsp;
went to go talk to Tommy one more time before&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:00.960 --> 00:15:04.240
the big event. She waited outside one of&nbsp;
his classes so she could let him know that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:04.240 --> 00:15:08.640
she’d have to be in by 11:30PM as not to&nbsp;
upset her mother more than she already had.

00:15:08.640 --> 00:15:12.400
Tommy thoughtfully suggest that after the&nbsp;
dance they go to the Kelly Fruit to get a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:12.400 --> 00:15:16.080
root beer and a burger. He figured it would be&nbsp;
a good place to unwind, since many of the other&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:16.080 --> 00:15:19.600
kids would be going to after parties in other&nbsp;
cities, and it would probably mostly be empty.

00:15:19.600 --> 00:15:21.920
Sue would later comment on&nbsp;
the exchange in her book.

00:15:21.920 --> 00:15:24.800
“This is the girl they keep calling&nbsp;
a monster. I want you to keep that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:24.800 --> 00:15:27.840
firmly in mind. The girl who could&nbsp;
be satisfied with a hamburger and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:27.840 --> 00:15:31.440
a dime root beer after her only school&nbsp;
dance so her momma wouldn't be worried…”

00:15:31.440 --> 00:15:36.400
The day that Carrie would first put on the&nbsp;
dress would soon come. It was May 27th 1969.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:36.400 --> 00:15:40.640
As Carrie examined herself in it, the door would&nbsp;
swings open to reveal her mother holding a bible.

00:15:40.640 --> 00:15:44.160
MARGARET: “Red, I might&nbsp;
have known it would be red.”

00:15:44.160 --> 00:15:47.680
The red dress is symbolic of everything that&nbsp;
this night stands for. Prom night is the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:47.680 --> 00:15:51.360
night that high school students dress up like&nbsp;
adults, practice the rituals of courtship,and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:51.360 --> 00:15:58.640
in most cases do adult things afterwards. Like&nbsp;
paying taxes….. ok no, were talking about se--

00:15:58.640 --> 00:16:02.400
The red dress is the perfect metaphor for that,&nbsp;
because it was the red blood of Carrie's first&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:02.400 --> 00:16:06.720
period that made her transition into adulthood&nbsp;
evident. And from her Mother's point of view, as I&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:06.720 --> 00:16:11.360
pointed out in my Things You Missed episode on the&nbsp;
1976 movie, red is also the color of the devil.

00:16:11.360 --> 00:16:15.040
Carrie did not know if her powers came from&nbsp;
Satan or if they were a gift from the Lord,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:15.040 --> 00:16:16.560
but she was beginning not to care,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:16.560 --> 00:16:20.000
and would use her powers against her mom&nbsp;
in order to attend the prom if necessary.

00:16:20.000 --> 00:16:24.080
Margaret asked her to burn the dress, and pray&nbsp;
for forgiveness with her, which of course angers&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:24.080 --> 00:16:27.680
Carrie. Ironically, the dress would be one&nbsp;
of the few things at the prom to not burn.

00:16:27.680 --> 00:16:31.520
Carrie uses her mind to swing the door shut&nbsp;
on her mother, who goes down to go to work.

00:16:31.520 --> 00:16:34.800
That night, Mrs. White spends at least&nbsp;
two hours praying in their home chapel,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:34.800 --> 00:16:38.000
so Carrie is forced to pin the corsage&nbsp;
to the shoulder of her dress herself,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:38.000 --> 00:16:42.160
an image that is indicative of how she was&nbsp;
now truly alone with nobody to turn to.

00:16:42.160 --> 00:16:46.720
As it got later, Carrie got more nervous. Thoughts&nbsp;
creep into her head about Tommy standing her up,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:46.720 --> 00:16:49.280
and she actually starts to think&nbsp;
that this would be for the best.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:49.280 --> 00:16:53.280
There would only be one more month of high school,&nbsp;
so the humiliation wouldn't last all that long.

00:16:53.280 --> 00:16:55.840
But then she thinks about being&nbsp;
stuck with her mother forever,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:55.840 --> 00:16:59.600
about going over to the 86 year-old Mrs.&nbsp;
Garrison's house and watching game shows&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:59.600 --> 00:17:01.920
and soap operas rather than starting her own life.

00:17:01.920 --> 00:17:05.360
Carrie is restlessly picking up objects with&nbsp;
her mind and putting them back down on the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:05.360 --> 00:17:09.440
ground when she hears Tommy's car approach. her&nbsp;
mother's chanting stops as hearings the buzzer.

00:17:11.680 --> 00:17:14.800
When Carrie answers the door neither&nbsp;
one of them says a word at first,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:14.800 --> 00:17:18.640
until she asks "do you like me?" And&nbsp;
he replies with, "you're beautiful."

00:17:19.200 --> 00:17:21.120
With that, the two set off together,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:21.120 --> 00:17:24.510
not knowing that this would be&nbsp;
the final evening of their lives.

00:17:32.000 --> 00:17:36.080
When Tommy Ross pulled into the parking lot he&nbsp;
asked her if she was nervous, and she said yes,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:36.080 --> 00:17:40.640
but I think the next scene does a far better job&nbsp;
of communicating how nervous she actually was.

00:17:40.640 --> 00:17:43.520
Everyone stopped to look at Tommy&nbsp;
and Carrie as they entered the prom,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:43.520 --> 00:17:46.320
creating a momentary silence that&nbsp;
was only broken by Tommy’s buddy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:46.320 --> 00:17:49.760
Geroge Dawson coming up and throwing&nbsp;
a mock insult about his appearance.

00:17:49.760 --> 00:17:53.600
“Dawson lurched forward with his fists up,&nbsp;
and for a moment Carrie felt stark terror.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:53.600 --> 00:17:56.960
In her keyed-up state, she came within&nbsp;
an ace of picking George up and throwing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:56.960 --> 00:18:01.280
him across the lobby. Then she realized it&nbsp;
was an old game, often played, well-loved.”

00:18:01.280 --> 00:18:05.520
Carrie was obviously very on edge, so&nbsp;
George’s date, Frieda tries to calm her&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:05.520 --> 00:18:09.280
by joking that she’ll dance with Carrie if&nbsp;
Tommy and George kill each other. She also&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:09.280 --> 00:18:12.640
asks Carrie about her dress and is very&nbsp;
impressed that Carrie made it herself.

00:18:12.640 --> 00:18:16.640
As the four of them go into the dance together&nbsp;
George is doing Flash Bobby Picket impressions.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:16.640 --> 00:18:19.840
What is with this Flash Bobby Picket?&nbsp;
This is like the third time he’s come up…

00:18:19.840 --> 00:18:22.080
When they entered, Carrie found&nbsp;
the dance to be glamorous,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:22.080 --> 00:18:25.520
and there’s a line where she specifically&nbsp;
views the long flowing dresses on the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:25.520 --> 00:18:29.760
dance floor to be like wraiths. Maybe that’s a&nbsp;
foreshadowing of all of their impending deaths.

00:18:29.760 --> 00:18:33.920
As Carrie, Tommy, George and Frieda admire the&nbsp;
mural, Carrie knew she’d remember the moment&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:33.920 --> 00:18:38.240
forever, but perhaps what she did not know, was&nbsp;
that “forever” would only be a few more hours.

00:18:38.240 --> 00:18:41.760
George takes Frieda onto the dance floor&nbsp;
and Tommy and Carrie decide to sit down.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:41.760 --> 00:18:44.400
One of the bullies, a girl named&nbsp;
Norma takes them to their table,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:44.400 --> 00:18:48.880
asking about Carrie’s dress as she does so.&nbsp;
Norma comments on how different Carrie looks,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:48.880 --> 00:18:53.360
the one time in her life that she actually fits&nbsp;
in for a short while. But Carrie notices something&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:53.360 --> 00:18:57.680
of a secretive look on Norma’s face, and that&nbsp;
makes Carrie nervous -- and for a good reason.

00:18:57.680 --> 00:19:01.840
Norma was part of a conspiracy created by&nbsp;
Chris Hargensen’s clique of girls known as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:01.840 --> 00:19:06.240
the Mortimer Snerds who planned to humiliate&nbsp;
Carrie by getting her elected as Prom Queen,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:06.240 --> 00:19:10.240
where Hargensen would pull the cord to have a&nbsp;
bucket of pig’s blood dumped all over Carrie.

00:19:10.240 --> 00:19:13.920
Tommy asked Carrie to dance, but she told him&nbsp;
she wanted to just sit for a while. In reality,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:13.920 --> 00:19:16.800
she had no idea how to dance and&nbsp;
wanted to avoid the embarrassment.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:16.800 --> 00:19:20.400
She asks Tommy to light the candles at their&nbsp;
table, which may be another foreshadowing,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:20.400 --> 00:19:22.880
this time about how the night would end in flames.

00:19:22.880 --> 00:19:27.440
At 9PM that evening, Tommy asked Carrie to dance&nbsp;
for a third time, and she finally admitted that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:27.440 --> 00:19:32.080
she did not know how. They end up waiting for a slower&nbsp;
song, and that’s a scene that’s in most if not all&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:32.080 --> 00:19:35.920
of the movie adaptations, but what the movies&nbsp;
fail to explain is that the dancing isn’t the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:35.920 --> 00:19:40.080
only thing that makes Carrie uncomfortable, she&nbsp;
is also bothered by the idea of going out there to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:40.080 --> 00:19:43.920
rock and roll music, which is something Carrie’s&nbsp;
mother has conditioned her to see as sinful.

00:19:43.920 --> 00:19:46.880
And if that’s true I’m going straight&nbsp;
to the bottom layer of hell…&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:47.680 --> 00:19:49.280
I probably am anyways, let's be real.

00:19:49.280 --> 00:19:52.160
They go around to talk to some of the other&nbsp;
tables and Carrie sees people bringing out&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:52.160 --> 00:19:55.280
the King and Queen thrones and she thinks&nbsp;
that they are beautiful and imagines her&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:55.280 --> 00:19:58.640
and Tommy winning the crown. Maybe this&nbsp;
was just her imagination running wild,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:58.640 --> 00:20:02.480
because she’s obviously not going to be a popular&nbsp;
choice without intervention, but maybe this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:02.480 --> 00:20:06.560
was actually her ‘shining’ and seeing a little&nbsp;
glimpse of that future where they are victorious.

00:20:06.560 --> 00:20:09.360
When they get back to the table, Tommy&nbsp;
goes to get her a little bit of punch,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:09.360 --> 00:20:13.520
and Carrie sees the gym teacher Ms. Desjardin, who&nbsp;
tells her about her own experience at the prom,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:13.520 --> 00:20:17.520
how she had been taller than her date, how the&nbsp;
corsage he’d given her had clashed with her gown,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:17.520 --> 00:20:19.840
and how the broken tailpipe on&nbsp;
the car made a horrible noise...

00:20:19.840 --> 00:20:24.500
TAILPIPE: "What's up guys, it's Tana Mongeau."

00:20:24.500 --> 00:20:27.440
...but that she still found it to&nbsp;
be a magical night. I only bring&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:27.440 --> 00:20:30.560
this up because they’ve changed this&nbsp;
story in literally every adaptation…

00:20:30.737 --> 00:20:34.780
MS. COLLINS: "I had a date with the captain of the basketball team."

00:20:34.780 --> 00:20:42.482
He was 6 feet 7 inches tall. Anyway, we went in his pickup truck. Which of course broke down. And we had to get out and walk the last half mile to the prom."

00:20:42.482 --> 00:20:46.551
MS. DESJARDIN: "My date brought a toy gun so he could pose like James Bond for the picture."

00:20:46.551 --> 00:20:50.105
CARRIE: "Oh, he sounds like fun!"

00:20:50.105 --> 00:20:58.314
MS. DESJARDIN: "Yeah. They arrested him. I didn't have anybody to dance with. Spent the entire night alone until my father picked me up."

00:20:58.480 --> 00:21:02.240
Anyway, Carrie tells Ms. Desjardin that she&nbsp;
couldn’t quite tell how the prom made her feel.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:02.240 --> 00:21:06.400
Tommy comes back with the punch, and Carrie&nbsp;
thinks the encounter with Ms. Desjardin’s was her way of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:06.400 --> 00:21:09.200
saying she’s sorry for everything&nbsp;
that happened in the locker room.

00:21:09.200 --> 00:21:12.880
At 9:30, the class president Vic Mooney,&nbsp;
who would be one of the few survivors of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:12.880 --> 00:21:16.320
the Black Prom, announces the opening&nbsp;
of the ballots for Prom King and Queen.

00:21:16.320 --> 00:21:19.680
Carrie is surprised to see her and Tommy’s&nbsp;
name on the ballot, which Tommy explains&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:19.680 --> 00:21:23.440
as the school voting for single candidates&nbsp;
and their dates getting shanghaied into it.”

00:21:23.440 --> 00:21:27.440
Tommy suggest they vote for themselves, and&nbsp;
Carrie giggles. When she does so she’s surprised&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:27.440 --> 00:21:30.800
at the sound of her own laughter, which is one of&nbsp;
those things where if you think about it, that’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:30.800 --> 00:21:36.560
incredibly sad, because she’s never had friends,&nbsp;
and so never really laughed even in her entire life. And&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:36.560 --> 00:21:40.880
I’m not gonna play the clip, don’t worry I’m not&nbsp;
gonna play the clip… but it was before this video…

00:21:40.880 --> 00:21:43.040
So there were less reasons to laugh in the world.

00:21:43.040 --> 00:21:46.720
While filling out the ballot, she accidentally&nbsp;
hurts herself as the pencil breaks in her hand.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:46.720 --> 00:21:49.232
Like the small candles, I think&nbsp;
the small amount of blood that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:49.232 --> 00:21:52.400
is drawn is tiny preview of the&nbsp;
splashdown that would soon come.

00:21:52.400 --> 00:21:54.480
The Honors Society collects the ballots and the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:54.480 --> 00:21:57.600
students watch as two piles stack&nbsp;
up higher than any of the others,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:57.600 --> 00:22:02.160
and eventually it is announced that Ewen High&nbsp;
School has had it’s first ever tie. Sixty-three&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:02.160 --> 00:22:06.880
votes for Frank Grier and Jessica MacLean and&nbsp;
sixty-three votes for Tommy Ross and Carrie White.

00:22:06.880 --> 00:22:11.280
They decide to hold a run-off ballot to determine&nbsp;
the winner. This time, Carrie begged Tommy not to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:11.280 --> 00:22:15.520
vote for them, perhaps sensing that something was&nbsp;
going to go wrong, but Tommy had promised Sue to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:15.520 --> 00:22:19.440
try to give Carrie the best night possible,&nbsp;
so he elects to try to vote her in anyways.

00:22:19.440 --> 00:22:23.040
It was 10:07PM when the secondary&nbsp;
ballots were collected, and again,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:23.040 --> 00:22:27.840
it looked like it was going to be close. Tommy and&nbsp;
Carrie end up winning by just one vote. Had Tommy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:27.840 --> 00:22:31.680
listened to Carrie and held back his vote, perhaps&nbsp;
the whole disaster could have been avoided.

00:22:31.680 --> 00:22:34.800
OK, so I was actually curious about&nbsp;
what would happen if it was a tie again,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:34.800 --> 00:22:38.160
so I looked it up and found some random&nbsp;
school in Ohio that had their rules posted&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:38.160 --> 00:22:41.760
online. They said they’d also institute a&nbsp;
second vote if the initial poll is tied,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:41.760 --> 00:22:44.160
and then if that one is tied,&nbsp;
there can be multiple winners.

00:22:44.160 --> 00:22:46.480
Though I feel like Hargensen still&nbsp;
probably would have dumped the blood&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:46.480 --> 00:22:49.600
just to get revenge on Carrie for&nbsp;
getting her in trouble at gym class.

00:22:49.600 --> 00:22:52.720
Ushers would appear to lead Carrie&nbsp;
and Tommy to their thrones while the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:52.720 --> 00:22:55.600
band played the school song. When they&nbsp;
took their place in front of the crowd,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:55.600 --> 00:22:59.520
everything had fallen into place for Christine&nbsp;
Hargensen, and although she hesitates at first,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:59.520 --> 00:23:03.280
she pulls the cord, which turns through the&nbsp;
pulley and attaches to the two buckets of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:23:03.280 --> 00:23:07.840
blood sitting on the rafters above&nbsp;
the Prom King and Queen thrones.

00:23:15.840 --> 00:23:20.240
After the massive red splash came down, Carrie&nbsp;
looked like she’d been dipped in red paint.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:23:20.240 --> 00:23:22.720
For a moment, the gymnasium was completely silent.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:23:22.720 --> 00:23:26.400
The two buckets clanged together and one of&nbsp;
them came down and hit Tommy in the head.

00:23:27.520 --> 00:23:31.440
“And the winner, by split&nbsp;
decision is.... THE BUCKET!”

00:23:35.760 --> 00:23:39.040
Someone started to laugh at the noise the&nbsp;
bucket made when it knocked out Tommy,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:23:39.040 --> 00:23:41.280
but it wasn’t until Carrie&nbsp;
opened her eyes back up,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:23:41.280 --> 00:23:44.560
the only part of her that was not red,&nbsp;
that everyone started to crack up,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:23:44.560 --> 00:23:48.480
but they’d soon find out that Carrie White&nbsp;
would be the one to have the last laught.

00:23:48.480 --> 00:23:51.840
Ms. Desjardin ran up to her aid, and&nbsp;
although she was not laughing on the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:23:51.840 --> 00:23:55.040
surface, Carrie could hear the giggling&nbsp;
reverberate through the gym teacher’s head,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:23:55.040 --> 00:23:58.640
so she uses her TK to push her aside&nbsp;
where she goes crashing into the wall.

00:23:58.640 --> 00:24:02.000
Carrie ran through the crowd, where someone&nbsp;
tripped her; she crawled away and ran out of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:24:02.000 --> 00:24:06.320
gym, out of the lobby, down the stairs and outside&nbsp;
of the school. With the laughter behind her now,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:24:06.320 --> 00:24:10.640
she got her feet tangled and fell into the grass.&nbsp;
The whole thing had only been about two minutes.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:24:10.640 --> 00:24:14.720
She was filled with tears, and her first instinct&nbsp;
was to return home to her mother in shame.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:24:14.720 --> 00:24:19.200
And had Mrs. White treated her daughter better,&nbsp;
that may have been the end it. But then again,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:24:19.200 --> 00:24:22.000
if that had been the case, probably&nbsp;
none of this would have happened.

00:24:22.000 --> 00:24:25.600
Carrie thinks about the closet, about how&nbsp;
long she would be locked in it this time.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:24:25.600 --> 00:24:29.120
About what her mother would do to her. And&nbsp;
that is what made her snap. Just as she&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:24:29.120 --> 00:24:33.520
did to little Tommy Urpter on the bicycle,&nbsp;
Carrie decided to use her powers for evil.

00:24:33.520 --> 00:24:38.160
She ditches her shoes and walks barefoot back to&nbsp;
the lobby, and all at once she slams the doors&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:24:38.160 --> 00:24:42.880
shut. The screams she heard from inside were&nbsp;
described as being like sweet soul music. The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:24:42.880 --> 00:24:46.560
panicked crowd stampedes towards the doors,&nbsp;
where Carrie stares back at them through the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:24:46.560 --> 00:24:50.960
window. People battered against the doors which&nbsp;
did not budge. Some went out the back fire doors,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:24:50.960 --> 00:24:54.320
and Carrie allowed them to escape, thinking&nbsp;
she’ll have time to pick them off later.

00:24:54.320 --> 00:24:58.320
She uses her mind to turn on the overhead&nbsp;
sprinklers, and when everyone was soaking wet,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:24:58.320 --> 00:25:02.160
Carrie could not hear them crying, so she&nbsp;
decided that the sprinklers were not enough.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:25:02.160 --> 00:25:06.000
He pulled out the power cables into the puddles&nbsp;
of water that now covered the gym floor,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:25:06.000 --> 00:25:09.360
causing a huge flash of light and the&nbsp;
electrocution of one of the performers&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:25:09.360 --> 00:25:13.200
holding onto a microphone stand. After another&nbsp;
flash of light, his shirt had caught fire and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:25:13.200 --> 00:25:17.200
one of the main power switches backstage&nbsp;
exploded. Light cables writhed in the air,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:25:17.200 --> 00:25:20.800
and one of them came down into the&nbsp;
water, causing yet another violent flash.

00:25:20.800 --> 00:25:24.480
Carrie went back down the stairs, all while&nbsp;
holding the main doors closed with her mind.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:25:24.480 --> 00:25:28.640
With the entire gym on fire now, she made her&nbsp;
way onto the street. The town fire whistle&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:25:28.640 --> 00:25:32.480
sounded and I think this is what caused her to&nbsp;
momentarily lose her hold on the doors, but she&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:25:32.480 --> 00:25:36.640
quickly regained it and slammed them back shut,&nbsp;
catching someone’s fingers inside as she did so.

00:25:36.640 --> 00:25:39.440
The movies always seem to under&nbsp;
appreciate the damage that Carrie&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:25:39.440 --> 00:25:42.080
did to the town after leaving the&nbsp;
high school for the last time.

00:25:42.080 --> 00:25:46.320
She headed into town and had the realization that&nbsp;
the fire department may put out her creation,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:25:46.320 --> 00:25:49.840
so she telekinetically twisted the fire&nbsp;
hydrant lugnuts, perhaps the most mentally&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:25:49.840 --> 00:25:54.080
draining use her power yet, based on how it&nbsp;
is described. She’s able to open the valves&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:25:54.080 --> 00:25:58.640
and water bursts everywhere. Carrie’s heartbeat&nbsp;
speeds up as she realizes she’s essentially won.

00:25:58.640 --> 00:26:02.400
The gushing water is a symbol that connects&nbsp;
the shower scene where Carrie was hurt and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:26:02.400 --> 00:26:07.120
humiliated to the rampage scene, where Carrie&nbsp;
pays that back to the entire town of Chamberlain.

00:26:07.120 --> 00:26:11.040
She goes to the grass plaza, where she’s seen&nbsp;
trying to rub her hands clean on the side of her&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:26:11.040 --> 00:26:15.600
dress, and she opens a few more fire hydrants up&nbsp;
before heading to the gas station, Teddy’s Amaco.

00:26:15.600 --> 00:26:18.160
She got there just before 11&nbsp;
o’clock, and she removed all&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:26:18.160 --> 00:26:20.640
of the nozzles and made them&nbsp;
pour gas onto the ground,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:26:20.640 --> 00:26:24.874
until someone unknowingly dropped a cigarette.&nbsp;
This caused a massive oil tank explosion,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:26:24.874 --> 00:26:24.960
which killed one off the police officers on&nbsp;
duty that night who happened to be nearby.

00:26:24.960 --> 00:26:29.440
Shortly after, at 11:12PM, Carrie had the&nbsp;
entirety of Main St. in flames. Her next&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:26:29.440 --> 00:26:33.760
target was the other gas station in town,&nbsp;
Tony’s Citgo, which exploded at 11:15. The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:26:33.760 --> 00:26:38.160
blast was so big that it temporarily lit up all&nbsp;
of Summer Street in what looked like daylight.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:26:38.160 --> 00:26:40.560
This was followed by another secondary explosion.

00:26:40.560 --> 00:26:44.400
Her progress was slowed a little bit but not&nbsp;
halted when she stepped on a broken bottle&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:26:44.400 --> 00:26:47.040
in the street.&nbsp;
This was a small reminder that she is human,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:26:47.040 --> 00:26:50.960
despite her terrifying powers, and she too&nbsp;
could be hurt and bleed just like anyone else,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:26:50.960 --> 00:26:52.640
something that would soon come into play.

00:26:52.640 --> 00:26:57.200
She arrives at her next destination at 12:06AM&nbsp;
on the morning of the 28th, where she’s able to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:26:57.200 --> 00:27:01.520
use her mind to locate and open the gas main&nbsp;
underneath Jackson Street. Shortly after,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:27:01.520 --> 00:27:05.280
she’s seen going inside the Carlin Street&nbsp;
Church. This is purely speculation, but I think&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:27:05.280 --> 00:27:09.280
she had hoped to find the answer to one of the&nbsp;
last questions that had eluded her to this point:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:27:09.280 --> 00:27:13.440
was she really an agent of the devil, or were&nbsp;
her powers a gift from God? When she received&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:27:13.440 --> 00:27:17.600
no answer, she used a whirlwind of psychic&nbsp;
energy to destroy the inside of the church.

00:27:17.600 --> 00:27:21.040
She emerged from there at 12:11 and&nbsp;
telekinetically swings the doors shut&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:27:21.040 --> 00:27:24.640
behind her. She also took out power&nbsp;
transformers and dangled live wires&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:27:24.640 --> 00:27:25.360
onto the street.

00:27:25.360 --> 00:27:28.400
One of these cables even reached a&nbsp;
nearby house and set that on fire&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:27:28.400 --> 00:27:31.840
as well. And remember that gas valve she&nbsp;
opened on Jackson Street? Well at 12:17,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:27:32.480 --> 00:27:36.400
an ambulance attendant pitched a cigarette&nbsp;
butt out the window and set that ablaze too.

00:27:36.400 --> 00:27:39.920
See, if the regular dangers of smoking were&nbsp;
not enough to deter you, take Chamberlaine,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:27:39.920 --> 00:27:43.920
Maine in 1979 as an example. The damage&nbsp;
could have basically been cut in half if&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:27:43.920 --> 00:27:47.280
people weren’t lighting up. And this guy&nbsp;
was an ambulance attendant. He’s literally&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:27:47.280 --> 00:27:49.920
supposed to keep people healthy,&nbsp;
why does he even have a cigarette?

00:27:49.920 --> 00:27:54.320
It was not long after that when Prom turned into&nbsp;
Homecoming, because Carrie found herself back at&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:27:54.320 --> 00:27:58.880
the door of the small house on Carlin Street. The&nbsp;
lights were entirely shut off when she arrived,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:27:58.880 --> 00:28:02.320
the only illumination coming from the&nbsp;
raging fires approaching from the town.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:28:02.320 --> 00:28:05.440
Objects fell from the walls as she&nbsp;
got close, and when she arrived,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:28:05.440 --> 00:28:08.960
she blew the all of the living room windows&nbsp;
outward and slammed the kitchen door.

00:28:08.960 --> 00:28:12.400
Carrie is described to this point to have&nbsp;
completely lost touch with her humanity,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:28:12.400 --> 00:28:16.480
but being back in the presence of her mother may&nbsp;
have brought her back down to earth a little bit -- either&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:28:16.480 --> 00:28:20.160
that or she was starting to realize the severity&nbsp;
of what she had done -- because when she stepped&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:28:20.160 --> 00:28:24.400
into the house she was trembling and whispering&nbsp;
out for her Momma. Her dress was in tatters.

00:28:24.400 --> 00:28:26.640
Like the poem she handed in back in seventh grade,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:28:26.640 --> 00:28:30.240
her return home had a deeper meaning then&nbsp;
what was there on the surface, but the mother&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:28:30.240 --> 00:28:34.952
and daughter were both so mentally unhinged&nbsp;
that there was only one inevitable outcome.

00:28:46.800 --> 00:28:48.080
When the two confront each other,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:28:48.080 --> 00:28:52.054
Margaret hides the kitchen knife that she’s&nbsp;
spent the last several hours sharpening…

00:28:59.520 --> 00:29:03.760
Yeah calm down Margaret. She tells the story of&nbsp;
Carrie’s conception and the pregnancy, how she&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:29:03.760 --> 00:29:07.440
planned to slay the devil inside of her when&nbsp;
Carrie was born, which drives her crazy -- she&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:29:07.440 --> 00:29:11.126
channels her telekinetic anger into the plates&nbsp;
in the kitchen which they both hear exploding.

00:29:11.223 --> 00:29:12.480
Carrie was unable to follow&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:29:12.480 --> 00:29:15.600
through with what she planned to do to&nbsp;
her mother at first, and begged for help.

00:29:15.600 --> 00:29:19.680
I think many people would argue that Carrie was&nbsp;
not a monster, but rather a victim of her own&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:29:19.680 --> 00:29:23.920
circumstances, and if there is any evidence&nbsp;
of that, this part is probably an example.

00:29:23.920 --> 00:29:27.200
Margaret asks her to pray with her one&nbsp;
more time, but when Carrie bows her head,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:29:27.200 --> 00:29:31.120
Margaret brings the knife down over her.&nbsp;
Carrie seems to sense this at the last moment,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:29:31.120 --> 00:29:33.423
and mentally moves the trajectory of the knife.

00:29:33.423 --> 00:29:34.607
"Mom!!!!"

00:29:34.607 --> 00:29:36.400
The way Carrie kills her mom has got to be one of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:29:36.400 --> 00:29:39.840
the coolest uses of telekinesis that&nbsp;
I’ve seen anywhere, she tells her:

00:29:39.840 --> 00:29:41.520
“I'm going to give you a present, Momma.”

00:29:41.520 --> 00:29:45.600
Then she looks into her chest and slowly&nbsp;
brings her mother’s beating heart to a stop.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:29:45.600 --> 00:29:48.240
I just think that’s so metal, because&nbsp;
there’s basically nothing you can do&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:29:48.240 --> 00:29:51.040
to defend yourself against that.&nbsp;
Carrie could not stick around long,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:29:51.040 --> 00:29:54.080
because the flames from the fires in&nbsp;
town had spread as close as next door,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:29:54.080 --> 00:29:58.640
and the roof, which she had already destroyed one&nbsp;time
14 years ago with stones, was starting to ignite.

00:29:58.640 --> 00:29:59.834
Carrie slipped out the back door. &nbsp;

00:29:59.834 --> 00:30:04.000
She crosses through backyards and when she can&nbsp;
no longer walk she crawls up an embankment,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:30:04.000 --> 00:30:07.840
not stopping until 1:15AM when she arrived&nbsp;
at a roadhouse known as The Cavalier.

00:30:08.686 --> 00:30:10.913
TOMMY: "A bunch of people were going to The Cavalier after."

00:30:10.913 --> 00:30:14.480
It’s even suggested in the text that this could&nbsp;
be the same roadhouse where Ralph White had&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:30:14.480 --> 00:30:18.560
stopped the night Carrie was conceived, and&nbsp;
she’d crawled all of this way to destroy it.

00:30:18.560 --> 00:30:22.240
But her main motive, most likely, had&nbsp;
more to do with who was at The Cavalier:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:30:22.240 --> 00:30:26.240
Chris Hargensen and her boyfriend Billy Nolan who&nbsp;
had helped set up the buckets of blood. They had&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:30:26.240 --> 00:30:29.840
just heard about the disaster and gotten in&nbsp;
the car to flee, and when Billy turns on the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:30:29.840 --> 00:30:34.720
headlights, Chris screams because Carrie White&nbsp;
is standing there with a crazed look on her face.

00:30:34.720 --> 00:30:38.640
Instinctively, Billy just floors it, and as&nbsp;
they approach, they hear the words “Carrie,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:30:38.640 --> 00:30:41.280
Carrie, Carrie” being chanted&nbsp;
in their heads over and over.

00:30:41.280 --> 00:30:45.840
It seems that when Carrie’s sanity snapped, so&nbsp;
too did her ability to keep her shine inside&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:30:45.840 --> 00:30:48.880
her own head. Much of what we know&nbsp;
about her rampage through the town&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:30:48.880 --> 00:30:52.640
obviously doesn’t come from Carrie first hand,&nbsp;
but those who encountered her and lived to tell&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:30:52.640 --> 00:30:56.800
the tale could hear her thoughts as if she were&nbsp;
no longer a radio, but now, a radio station.

00:30:56.800 --> 00:30:59.600
It’s never spelled out for us how&nbsp;
this exactly works in the book,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:30:59.600 --> 00:31:01.600
but there is one point where Sue seems to believe&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:31:01.600 --> 00:31:05.200
that the “zone of Carrie’s influence” was&nbsp;
shrinking as she was starting to die.”

00:31:05.200 --> 00:31:08.240
If the unscrewing of the fire hydrants&nbsp;
wasn’t Carrie’s most impressive feat,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:31:08.240 --> 00:31:11.600
then what would come next definitely&nbsp;
is. She spun the car around in a half&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:31:11.600 --> 00:31:14.640
circle and sent it flying into The&nbsp;
Cavalier. Billy is thrown through&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:31:14.640 --> 00:31:18.200
the windshield as Chris crumbles against&nbsp;
the dashboard before the vehicle explodes.

00:31:18.560 --> 00:31:22.480
That seemed to take up the rest of Carrie’s&nbsp;
remaining energy. She laid on her side panting,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:31:22.480 --> 00:31:26.000
and tried to drag herself across the parking&nbsp;
lot. She felt that nothing would matter,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:31:26.000 --> 00:31:29.840
as long as she could turn herself over and&nbsp;
see the stars one last time before she died,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:31:29.840 --> 00:31:32.080
but she did not even have the strength to do that.

00:31:32.080 --> 00:31:35.280
The last person Carrie White&nbsp;
ever encounters is Sue Snell,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:31:35.280 --> 00:31:38.480
the one girl who tried to give Carrie&nbsp;
that one good high school experience&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:31:38.480 --> 00:31:42.000
at the prom, and the one person who&nbsp;
actually had her best interests in mind.

00:31:42.000 --> 00:31:45.680
Sue turned her on her back, her final&nbsp;
wish fulfilled, and Carrie in a moan,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:31:45.680 --> 00:31:49.920
asks who is there. When she finds out that it’s&nbsp;
Sue, Carrie accuses her of being in on the trick,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:31:49.920 --> 00:31:52.640
to which Sue asks her to look&nbsp;
inside of her and see the truth.

00:31:52.640 --> 00:31:55.440
Carrie does so, scanning the&nbsp;
library of Sue’s mind. The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:31:55.440 --> 00:31:58.640
concept of a metaphysical library or&nbsp;
warehouse of memories is consistent&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:31:58.640 --> 00:32:01.600
with some of King’s later writings&nbsp;
like Dreamcatcher and Doctor Sleep.

00:32:01.600 --> 00:32:05.760
Carrie searches through all of Sue’s thoughts&nbsp;
and memories, but finds no evidence of a plan to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:32:05.760 --> 00:32:10.160
sabotage her at the prom. With that last little&nbsp;
peace of mind, Carrie pulls back out of Sue’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:32:10.160 --> 00:32:14.720
head, but in what I can only imagine is some kind&nbsp;
of telekinetic equivalent of Newton’s Third Law,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:32:14.720 --> 00:32:18.880
Sue gets sucked into Carrie’s mind against&nbsp;
her will and perceives her final thoughts. She&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:32:18.880 --> 00:32:24.320
hears Carrie crying for her mother, and her last&nbsp;
conscious thought is: “Momma… I’m sorry…. Where--”&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:32:25.200 --> 00:32:26.960
before fading out into the black.

00:32:26.960 --> 00:32:32.720
Carrietta White’s official time of death is&nbsp;
recorded as May 28, 1979 at 2:00AM. Carrie was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:32:32.720 --> 00:32:36.800
one of King’s most misunderstood characters. If&nbsp;
you read the book, you get a better understanding&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:32:36.800 --> 00:32:41.040
of how Carrie was just a normal girl, but she’s&nbsp;
pushed into being an outcast by everyone around&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:32:41.040 --> 00:32:45.280
her, and the idea of her telekinesis and mind&nbsp;
reading abilities that seemingly nobody else&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:32:45.280 --> 00:32:49.520
has is a metaphor for her forced separation&nbsp;
from the rest of society. The concept would&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:32:49.520 --> 00:32:51.040
become a staple of the author’s work,

00:32:51.040 --> 00:32:55.120
But Stephen King has actually gone on record&nbsp;
saying that Brian DiPalma’s 1976 movie&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:32:55.120 --> 00:32:59.520
adaptation of Carrie is the superior version of&nbsp;
the story. DiPalma brings in many more concepts,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:32:59.520 --> 00:33:03.920
themes and motifs in his interpretation of&nbsp;
the tragic tale, so we decided to do a second&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:33:03.920 --> 00:33:08.000
video over on Amagi’s channel analysing&nbsp;
the life of Carrie White in the movie.

00:33:08.000 --> 00:33:11.120
And if you like Horror History,&nbsp;
definitely go subscribe to his channel,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:33:11.120 --> 00:33:14.080
he covers the lives of many other of&nbsp;
your favorite characters, including&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:33:14.080 --> 00:33:17.520
those outside of the horror genre. Remember&nbsp;
to ring that deathbell for notifications,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:33:17.520 --> 00:33:21.734
and I’ll see you over in that second&nbsp;
video. Assuming we both survive.

